# Testing Guidelines

## Testing Framework
The framework includes testing utilities in [Brain/Classes/Testing/](mdc:Brain/Classes/Testing/):
- [Brain/Classes/Testing/TestCase.php](mdc:Brain/Classes/Testing/TestCase.php) - Base test case
- [Brain/Classes/Testing/unittest.php](mdc:Brain/Classes/Testing/unittest.php) - Unit testing utilities
- [Brain/Classes/Testing/microtest.php](mdc:Brain/Classes/Testing/microtest.php) - Micro testing framework
- [Brain/Classes/Testing/PerformanceTest.php](mdc:Brain/Classes/Testing/PerformanceTest.php) - Performance testing

## Test Organization
Tests are organized in the [Tests/](mdc:Tests/) directory:
- Unit tests for individual classes and methods
- Integration tests for module interactions
- Functional tests for complete workflows
- Performance tests for optimization validation

## Testing Patterns

### Unit Testing
- Test individual methods and classes
- Use dependency injection for testability
- Mock external dependencies
- Test both success and failure scenarios
- Validate input and output data

### Integration Testing
- Test module interactions
- Validate database operations
- Test API endpoints
- Verify authentication flows
- Test error handling scenarios

### Functional Testing
- Test complete user workflows
- Validate end-to-end functionality
- Test form submissions
- Verify data persistence
- Test user interface interactions

## Test Data Management
- Use [Brain/Classes/Testing/TestDataFactory.php](mdc:Brain/Classes/Testing/TestDataFactory.php)
- Create realistic test data
- Use database fixtures
- Implement data cleanup
- Use consistent test data across tests

## Performance Testing
- Use [Brain/Classes/Testing/PerformanceTest.php](mdc:Brain/Classes/Testing/PerformanceTest.php)
- Measure response times
- Test under load conditions
- Monitor memory usage
- Validate optimization improvements

## Testing Best Practices

### Test Structure
- Follow Arrange-Act-Assert pattern
- Use descriptive test names
- Keep tests focused and simple
- Avoid test interdependencies
- Implement proper test isolation

### Test Coverage
- Aim for high code coverage
- Test edge cases and error conditions
- Validate security scenarios
- Test performance requirements
- Include accessibility testing

### Continuous Integration
- Run tests automatically on code changes
- Implement test result reporting
- Use automated deployment pipelines
- Monitor test execution times
- Implement test failure notifications

## Security Testing
- Test authentication mechanisms
- Validate authorization controls
- Test input validation
- Verify CSRF protection
- Test for common vulnerabilities

## Database Testing
- Use test database instances
- Implement database fixtures
- Test migration scripts
- Validate data integrity
- Test transaction handling

## API Testing
- Test all API endpoints
- Validate request/response formats
- Test error handling
- Verify authentication
- Test rate limiting

## Documentation Testing
- Validate code examples
- Test installation procedures
- Verify configuration examples
- Test troubleshooting guides
- Validate API documentation